Expected elements: present

Every Must-show item is on the page and carries real content: the affirmative `Real Aztec mainnet data` badge with `aztec-mainnet` beside it and the producer's own sentences, inset to the same column as the breadcrumb; the fixed nav with resolver field; the `Not observable` badge with the published pruning reason attributed to the chain's retention; the full hash, `Succeeded` badge and a complete Overview; Internal calls and State changes both in the permanent tense; the permanence claim verbatim; and a footer that ends the page with all three marks (heart, CodeTracer, GitHub) drawn and visible. No Debug/retry/spinner, no trace reference, no error tone. The COST row now reads `0x0000…f97278 mana (FeeJuice)` with no dangling separator.

In density terms the page is legible but under-loaded. At 1920 it is a single ~910px column with ~500px of dead canvas each side, running 2872px tall — 2.7 screens — and the fold at 1080px lands exactly on the top border of the Overview table, so a wide-screen reader sees the banner, hash and reason but not one metadata value. The COST row is the worst-value pixel on the page: 50 leading zeros of a padded 32-byte word occupy ~78% of the row width, and its label is the adapter's raw field name flattened to `TRANSACTIONFEE`, which wraps and doubles the row height.

Highest-priority fixes: format the fee as a decimal quantity with a readable label; use the wide breakpoint to pair Overview with Decoded input and set the three empty-section cards as a row.

Rating: 6/10

